<title>IRAN: Iran company to start oil drilling work in Libya.</title>
<headline>Iran company to start oil drilling work in Libya.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Iranian Drilling Company (NIDC) has opened a branch in Libya and is setting up oil drilling rigs in the North African country, a company official said in remarks published on Thursday.</p>
<p>NIDC General Manager Mohammad Javad Asemipour, quoted by the daily Kar va Kargar, said the state-owned firm recently opened its Libyan office and &quot;drilling equipment is being set up.&quot; He did not give further details.</p>
</text>
